r installs and reconciles the platform\n  correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster.\n- The Platform Operator build pipeline carries a gating FIPS check that\n  fails a build which reintroduces non-validated crypto usage and passes the\n  remediated builds (build pipeline green with the check in place).\n- The module inventory is updated to reflect the post-remediation state of\n  the Platform Operator image.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — primary: all serving-stack images run correctly on\n  FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (Platform Operator\n  image).\n- **HLR-3 (P1)** — bundled: the gating FIPS regression check for Platform\n  Operator builds is carried in this epic rather than a standalone\n  enforcement epic because it guards the exact build surface this epic\n  converts and shares its detection tooling and pipeline wiring — it is not\n  separately schedulable from the remediation of the same surface.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Remediation actions depend on the FIPS crypto audit's findings; if a\n  finding requires an upstream dependency release that is not yet available,\n  the remediation approach for the image is rewritten accordingly.\n- Security review board sign-off at defined milestones is a mandatory human\n  gate on the compliance program.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44029,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b38720daf7576781","agent_id":"ab6f27ed01cf429e6","session_id":"fe0d12c6-319a-4740-b115-3713d369a771","uuid":"e8dcbbdd-0161-44ca-b170-b4a1b4164724","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:15:28.830Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013 into epics"}
