{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-aaeeee1a-dfff-435c-8050-8057cf4a6b2f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d7e396602185348","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-7gqf0n6c/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E004.md","content":"# FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package assembly and submission\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic assembles the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model\nserving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and test results — and\nsubmits it through the security review board to the external accredited\ncertification lab. The strategy currently has no compliance evidence package;\nthis epic produces it from the outputs of the serving-stack FIPS remediation\nand hands it off to the certification process.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Assemble the final module inventory from the FIPS crypto audit and the\n  post-remediation inventory updates for the KServe images and the Platform\n  Operator image.\n- Collect build attestations for every remediated serving-stack image from\n  its build pipeline.\n- Collect the FIPS-enabled cluster validation test results for the\n  remediated KServe images and the Platform Operator image.\n- Compose the package to the certification lab's submission requirements\n  (inventory, attestations, test results, and supporting documentation).\n- Submit the package through the security review board and hand it off to\n  the external certification lab; track it through the submission\n  milestone.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The evidence package contains the complete module inventory, build\n  attestations for every remediated serving-stack image, and the\n  FIPS-enabled cluster test results for the serving stack.\n- The package passes an internal completeness review against the\n  certification lab's submission requirements before hand-off (every\n  required element present; a missing element is a failure).\n- The package is submitted through the security review board and handed off\n  to the external certification lab, with the submission recorded and\n  tracked.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — primary: the compliance evidence package (module\n  inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted\n  through the security review board to the external certification lab.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Certification lab turnaround is historically six to nine months and the\n  security review board meets on a fixed cadence; both are externally\n  controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. They are\n  schedule risks on this epic, not acceptance criteria — this epic's\n  engineering completion point is the assembled, internally validated, and\n  submitted package.\n- Certification outcome (lab approval) is beyond this strategy's HLR-2\n  completion point (submission) and is tracked as a program risk.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44827,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b38720daf7576781","agent_id":"ab6f27ed01cf429e6","session_id":"fe0d12c6-319a-4740-b115-3713d369a771","uuid":"e9ac4291-ab42-4336-87f8-7569e55068f3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:15:38.943Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013 into epics"}
