{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8de3c25e99417625","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: FIPS crypto usage audit and remediation-path investigation for serving-stack\n4\t  images\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n6\tcomponent: KServe\n7\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 1\n14\t  local_runnability: 1\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n16\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# FIPS crypto usage audit and remediation-path investigation for serving-stack images\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the central unknown of the FIPS 140-3 compliance\n31\teffort for the model serving stack: which serving-stack images — the KServe\n32\tcomponent images and the Platform Operator image — link non-validated\n33\tcryptographic libraries, and what the validated-crypto remediation path is for\n34\teach finding. Its deliverable is a complete module inventory (the seed of the\n35\tcompliance evidence package) and a per-image remediation plan that the\n36\tremediation work for each component builds on. The remediation direction is\n37\tfixed by the strategy (remove non-validated crypto from the request path), but\n38\twhich images, which libraries, and which replacements apply is not yet known —\n39\tthe answer changes what the downstream remediation work does.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Enumerate every serving-stack image in scope: all KServe component images\n44\t  and the Platform Operator image.\n45\t- For each image, identify the cryptographic libraries and modules linked\n46\t  into it (base images, language runtimes, vendored dependencies) and classify\n47\t  each as validated or non-validated for FIPS 140-3 purposes.\n48\t- Determine a remediation path for every non-validated finding: validated\n49\t  replacement library or base image, dependency upgrade, or rebuild with\n50\t  FIPS-appropriate build configuration.\n51\t- Identify findings whose remediation requires changes in upstream projects\n52\t  (dependency releases, upstream patches), including what the upstream change\n53\t  is and who owns it.\n54\t- Produce the module inventory and per-image remediation plan as a reviewable\n55\t  artifact, handed to the per-component remediation work.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A module inventory exists that covers every in-scope serving-stack image\n60\t  and lists, per image, the linked crypto modules with their\n61\t  validated/non-validated classification — a image omitted from the inventory\n62\t  is a failure.\n63\t- Every non-validated finding in the inventory has an identified remediation\n64\t  path naming the validated replacement (library, base image, or build\n65\t  configuration change).\n66\t- Findings requiring upstream changes are listed with the upstream project,\n67\t  the change needed, and whether a midstream workaround exists.\n68\t- The remediation plan is handed off to the per-component remediation work\n69\t  with per-image actions such that each component team can start without\n70\t  re-deriving the analysis.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — enables: the audit determines which images must be\n75\t  remediated and how; the remediation epics for KServe and the Platform\n76\t  Operator are gated on this outcome.\n77\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — partial: the module inventory produced here is a required\n78\t  input of the compliance evidence package.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-899ae1005764a1dd","agent_id":"a138c43316943d2b2","session_id":"fe0d12c6-319a-4740-b115-3713d369a771","uuid":"04c