remediation plan to the Platform Operator image: swap\n51\t  non-validated crypto libraries and base images for validated ones, upgrade\n52\t  or rebuild dependencies, and adjust build configuration as the plan\n53\t  specifies.\n54\t- Update the module inventory entry for the remediated Platform Operator\n55\t  image so the compliance evidence package reflects the post-remediation\n56\t  state.\n57\t- Add a gating FIPS regression check to the Platform Operator build pipeline\n58\t  that fails any Platform Operator build reintroducing non-validated crypto\n59\t  usage (this epic owns the enforcement for the Platform Operator image\n60\t  surfaces it converts).\n61\t- Validate the remediated image on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster: the\n62\t  operator installs and reconciles the platform correctly with the request\n63\t  path using validated crypto.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- The Platform Operator image contains no non-validated crypto in the\n68\t  request path, verified by re-running the audit's scanning method on the\n69\t  remediated image.\n70\t- The remediated Platform Operator installs and reconciles the platform\n71\t  correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster.\n72\t- The Platform Operator build pipeline carries a gating FIPS check that\n73\t  fails a build which reintroduces non-validated crypto usage and passes the\n74\t  remediated builds (build pipeline green with the check in place).\n75\t- The module inventory is updated to reflect the post-remediation state of\n76\t  the Platform Operator image.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — primary: all serving-stack images run correctly on\n81\t  FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (Platform Operator\n82\t  image).\n83\t- **HLR-3 (P1)** — bundled: the gating FIPS regression check for Platform\n84\t  Operator builds is carried in this epic rather than a standalone\n85\t  enforcement epic because it guards the exact build surface this epic\n86\t  converts and shares its detection tooling and pipeline wiring — it is not\n87\t  separately schedulable from the remediation of the same surface.\n88\t\n89\t## Risks / Notes\n90\t\n91\t- Remediation actions depend on the FIPS crypto audit's findings; if a\n92\t  finding requires an upstream dependency release that is not yet available,\n93\t  the remediation approach for the image is rewritten accordingly.\n94\t- Security review board sign-off at defined milestones is a mandatory human\n95\t  gate on the compliance program.\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-899ae1005764a1dd","agent_id":"a138c43316943d2b2","session_id":"fe0d12c6-319a-4740-b115-3713d369a771","uuid":"5c7318b8-8784-4db1-b929-6a6f79933ff5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:17:35.609Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6d5e36d6937a253","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
