{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88c114f19cf05de3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E004\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package assembly and submission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 0\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: -1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Low\n25\tai_implementability_score: -1\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package assembly and submission\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic assembles the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model\n36\tserving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and test results — and\n37\tsubmits it through the security review board to the external accredited\n38\tcertification lab. The strategy currently has no compliance evidence package;\n39\tthis epic produces it from the outputs of the serving-stack FIPS remediation\n40\tand hands it off to the certification process.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Assemble the final module inventory from the FIPS crypto audit and the\n45\t  post-remediation inventory updates for the KServe images and the Platform\n46\t  Operator image.\n47\t- Collect build attestations for every remediated serving-stack image from\n48\t  its build pipeline.\n49\t- Collect the FIPS-enabled cluster validation test results for the\n50\t  remediated KServe images and the Platform Operator image.\n51\t- Compose the package to the certification lab's submission requirements\n52\t  (inventory, attestations, test results, and supporting documentation).\n53\t- Submit the package through the security review board and hand it off to\n54\t  the external certification lab; track it through the submission\n55\t  milestone.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- The evidence package contains the complete module inventory, build\n60\t  attestations for every remediated serving-stack image, and the\n61\t  FIPS-enabled cluster test results for the serving stack.\n62\t- The package passes an internal completeness review against the\n63\t  certification lab's submission requirements before hand-off (every\n64\t  required element present; a missing element is a failure).\n65\t- The package is submitted through the security review board and handed off\n66\t  to the external certification lab, with the submission recorded and\n67\t  tracked.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — primary: the compliance evidence package (module\n72\t  inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted\n73\t  through the security review board to the external certification lab.\n74\t\n75\t## Risks / Notes\n76\t\n77\t- Certification lab turnaround is historically six to nine months and the\n78\t  security review board meets on a fixed cadence; both are externally\n79\t  controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. They are\n80\t  schedule risks on this epic, not acceptance criteria — this epic's\n81\t  engineering completion point is the assembled, internally validated, and\n82\t  submitted package.\n83\t- Certification outcome (lab approval) is beyond this strategy's HLR-2\n84\t  completion point (submission) and is tracked as a program risk.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-899ae1005764a1dd","agent_id":"a138c43316943d2b2","session_id":"fe0d12c6-319a-4740-b115-3713d369a771","uuid":"5c4b743a-7b20-4652-9c31-2ea14e3299fe","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:17:36.379Z","tool_result